# Local development secrets for `npm run dev` (Vite + workerd).
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the keys you actually have.
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored; this example file is not, so never put a real key
# in here.
#
# IMPORTANT: these are read by the Worker (c.env), NOT by Vite. Do not move
# them into `.env` and do not prefix them with VITE_ - anything named VITE_* is
# inlined into the browser bundle, which would publish your key.
#
# In production these are Wrangler secrets instead:
#   npx wrangler secret put POE_API_KEY

# --- Keys: one per upstream account ----------------------------------------

# OpenCode Go (https://opencode.ai/go) - serves ChatGPT (GPT 5.6 Luna),
# DeepSeek, Grok, and the free MiMo and Muse Spark tiers by default. One key,
# two protocols behind it. Muse Spark needs a one-time data-collection opt-in
# in the OpenCode workspace, or it answers 403 DataPolicyError.
OPENCODE_API_KEY=

# Poe (https://poe.com/api_key) - serves Claude and Gemini by default; can also
# serve ChatGPT (CHATGPT_CHANNEL=poe).
POE_API_KEY=

# Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) - only needed when
# GEMINI_CHANNEL is set to "google".
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- Optional local overrides ----------------------------------------------
# Anything in wrangler.jsonc "vars" can be overridden here for local runs,
# for example:
#   GEMINI_CHANNEL=google
#   CHATGPT_CHANNEL=poe
#   POE_CHATGPT_MODEL=gpt-5.4-pro
#   OPENCODE_GROK_MODEL=grok-4.5
#   NO_STREAM=deepseek                # only needed on the free Workers plan (10 ms CPU)
#
# Check a key without spending tokens:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $POE_API_KEY" https://api.poe.com/v1/models
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENCODE_API_KEY" -H "x-opencode-session: any-uuid" https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/models
# A 401 means the key itself is rejected; the model name is a separate problem
# and shows up as a 404 or an "unknown model" message.
